></div><div><br></div><div>As you probably know, there are quite a few situ=
ations in which endpoints close the connection before</div><div>receiving a=
 close_notify, for instance, when they receive an end of data message in th=
e application</div><div>protocol or when they time out. The former case is =
generally safe, the latter is not, but extremely</div><div>common, in fact =
perhaps the dominant case. Do we agree on that?</div><div><br></div><div>-E=
kr</div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=3D"gmail_quote"><div dir=3D"ltr=
